AB  - The skeletal extension and corallite shape of individuals of the Caribbean and Atlantic reef-building coral M. annularis (Ellis and Solander) were measured after more than 6 wk continuous flow-through exposure in laboratory aquaria to treatments of 0, 1, 10 and 100-ppm (.mu.l l-1) drilling mud. Linear increase of the skeleton (extension rate) and fossa length were significantly depressed in the 100-ppm drilling mud impairs coral skeletal growth rate and possibly interferes with sediment rejection capability by lowering calical relief.
